  </section>

  <section id="posle">
    <h2>After surgery</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>After planned surgery the hospital stay is usually about a week.</li>
      <li>Follow-up CT angiography — typically after a month: it shows the clip position and patency of the vessels.</li>
      <li>Blood pressure control and not smoking remain important after surgery.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="srochno" slot="urgent">
    <h2>When to seek urgent help</h2>
    <div class="callout alert">
      <p>A sudden "thunderclap" headache — the worst of your life, especially with vomiting, loss of consciousness or seizures — <strong>call emergency services immediately (112; 103 in Russia).</strong> Even if the pain has passed, it may have been a sentinel bleed.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
